course: dictionary
lesson: 8278
title: Working out a word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Context is the words around a word, and they often give you its meaning. In Alice in Wonderland, Alice says, «her hair goes in such long ringlets, and mine doesn't go in ringlets at all». Hair that goes in ringlets must be curly, so a ringlet must be a curl of some kind.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of the hard word. «Ada's hair goes in such long ringlets» still makes sense if you say «Ada's hair goes in such long curls». That is a good sign your guess is right.
explain: Pictures help too. Old pictures of Victorian girls often show long ringlets hanging down on each side of the face. Hairdressers make ringlets with curling tongs, which is another clue that ringlets are curls.
fact: A ringlet is a long, curly lock of hair hanging down in a spiral.
fact: A spiral is a shape that winds round and round, like a curl.
fact: Alice's hair does not go in ringlets, so her hair is not curled in that way.
fact: Hairdressers make ringlets with curling tongs.
fact: In stories and old pictures, ringlets often show Victorian girls.
exercise: What is a ringlet? | A wooden hairbrush | *A long, curly lock of hair hanging down in a spiral | A hat worn at the seaside | A short, straight hair clip
exercise: Alice says her hair does not go in ringlets. What can you tell about ringlets from this? | Alice's hair is curly like that already | *They are curls, and Alice's hair is not curly like that | They are a kind of hat
exercise: What do hairdressers make with curling tongs? | Pancakes | Maps | *Ringlets | Castles
test: In «Ada's hair goes in such long ringlets», what does ringlets mean? | Short cut hair | Hair tied up in a bun | *Long curly locks hanging in spirals | Hair shaved off completely
test: Which story has Alice worrying about ringlets? | Peter Pan | Treasure Island | Robinson Crusoe | *Alice in Wonderland
exam: Using the context of «Ada's hair goes in such long ringlets», which picture best matches a ringlet? | A bald head | A straight ponytail | *A long curl hanging down in a spiral | A tight bun on top of the head
